Bulgarian law contains no offence of hitchhiking (''автостоп''), and on ordinary roads it is legal. [https://www.rta.government.bg/upload/15545/zdvp.pdf Article 55(1) of the ''Закон за движението по пътищата''] allows onto a road signed as an ''автомагистрала'' or ''скоростен път'' only motor vehicles whose design speed exceeds 70 km/h, and forbids in the same sentence the movement of pedestrians, the leading of animals and the other categories barred by article 21 — a wording tightened by the amendment in force from 7 September 2025. Article 58(1) forbids a driver on a motorway to stop or park anywhere but the specially marked places, and to halt on the emergency lane except for a breakdown or a health problem. So the marked rest areas and their petrol stations are the only spot on the motorway where a lift can lawfully begin, and the carriageway, the shoulder and the slip road are closed to you. On first- and second-class roads and everything below, thumbing from the verge breaks no rule.
